Trajectory Inference Tool

DESCRIPTION:
This tool performs single-cell trajectory inference to identify developmental 
pathways, disease progression patterns, or temporal ordering in biological data.

FUNCTIONALITY:
- K-nearest neighbor graph construction
- Diffusion-based pseudotime computation
- Branch point detection
- Trajectory graph generation
- Lineage analysis
- Differential expression along trajectory

INPUT FORMAT:
1. data: 2D feature matrix (cells/samples x genes/features)
   - Rows are individual cells or samples
   - Columns are features (genes, measurements)
   - Example: [[0.5, 1.2, ...], [0.8, 1.1, ...], ...]

2. cell_ids: Optional list of cell/sample identifiers
   - Example: ["cell_1", "cell_2", ...]

3. root_cell: Optional index of root cell for trajectory

OUTPUT FORMAT:
{
    "pseudotime": {
        "values": [0.0, 0.15, 0.32, ...],
        "cell_ids": ["cell_1", "cell_2", ...]
    },
    "graph": {
        "nodes": [...],
        "edges": [...],
        "type": "trajectory_graph"
    },
    "branch_points": [
        {"pseudotime": 0.4, "confidence": 0.85}
    ]
}

USAGE NOTES:
- Data should be preprocessed (normalized, scaled)
- Root cell selection affects trajectory direction
- Branch detection sensitivity controlled by min_branch_length
- Supports multiple trajectory algorithms: monocle3, slingshot, paga

